title: "Allocating AI Translation Compute for Marginal Educational Access"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "OpenAI Codex Research"
date-released: "2026-08-31"
version: "1.1.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22217113
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22217113"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/allocating-ai-translation-compute-for-educational-access"
abstract: >-
  This report constructs a reproducible global portfolio model for allocating
  AI-assisted adaptation of open mathematics resources according to additional
  comfortable, usable educational access. It combines dated population evidence,
  exact language-variety-script-territory profiles, academic-language overlap,
  curriculum needs, accessibility, open-resource workloads, and evidence-bounded
  interlanguage architectures. The operational Top 10 begins with a Bangla
  shared-source package, Telugu, Odia, Bhojpuri, and Hausa. Bahasa Indonesia,
  Mainland Simplified Chinese, and Japanese are retained as explicit equal-basis
  profiles rather than silently omitted. The package preserves frozen inputs,
  needs-specific commissioning assignments, an Indonesian program audit, and
  deterministic validation receipts.
  Research synthesis, analysis, drafting, and reproducibility work used OpenAI
  Codex gpt-5.6-sol, Ultra.
keywords:
  - educational access
  - language of instruction
  - open educational resources
  - artificial intelligence
  - machine translation
  - low-resource languages
  - interlanguages
  - mathematics education
  - OpenStax
  - Open Logic Project
  - accessibility
  - cost-effectiveness
